{"parentUuid":"a9b1f37e-4131-447e-9ad7-6861721987f6","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f097ba1e-802d-4788-86d0-92157481e0f4","agentId":"ad35f6feb999bff94","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AFBRrHS7vFFVge33EbsMSH","type":"tool_result","content":"14:# Isometric Strength Gains Spread Further From the Training Angle When the Muscle Trains in a Lengthened Position\n20:up to about 15 degrees either side of the training angle. Because every type of muscle\n26:most lengthened: males training isometrically for 5 weeks (5 sets of 5 reps, 5 seconds each,\n27:3 times weekly) at 25 degrees of elbow flexion (full extension = 0 degrees) gained 54%\n29:group training at 80 degrees gained 30% at the training angle and about 25% over the rest of\n7:topic: joint angle training and strength transfer\n8:category: [joint-angle, transfer, exercise-selection]\n14:# Training at a Joint's Longest-Muscle-Length Angle Transfers More Evenly; Training at a Shortened Angle Gains More but Transfers Less\n18:training determines how that strength gain transfers to other joint angles. If maximum","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"9111ddf8-0c7d-4de8-99b4-6d724b1700b5","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:42:55.948Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"14:# Isometric Strength Gains Spread Further From the Training Angle When the Muscle Trains in a Lengthened Position\n20:up to about 15 degrees either side of the training angle. Because every type of muscle\n26:most lengthened: males training isometrically for 5 weeks (5 sets of 5 reps, 5 seconds each,\n27:3 times weekly) at 25 degrees of elbow flexion (full extension = 0 degrees) gained 54%\n29:group training at 80 degrees gained 30% at the training angle and about 25% over the rest of\n7:topic: joint angle training and strength transfer\n8:category: [joint-angle, transfer, exercise-selection]\n14:# Training at a Joint's Longest-Muscle-Length Angle Transfers More Evenly; Training at a Shortened Angle Gains More but Transfers Less\n18:traini