{"parentUuid":"156db810-b3d7-4117-8544-005742e2172e","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ad35f6feb999bff94","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CffVBg3pTkvLfvJsu8Z62","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Verdict: GO AFTER FIXES.** Of the 23 entries, 15 are GO, 8 need fixes and none are NO-GO. `_book.md` needs one fix as well.\n\nReport: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/review_supertraining_ch4-3-4_opus.md`\n\n**Required fixes:**\n1. **Power entry** (`claim--power-equals-force-times-velocity-only-when-force-is-constant`): the physics is wrong and it is rated `proven`. Moment-to-moment power is always force times velocity, even when force varies. The real caution is that an average or peak force times velocity is not power. It needs a new title, a narrower `proven` scope and a rewritten \"When NOT to apply\" line.\n2. **Five-criteria framework**: the inference says the criteria conflict and cites Fig 4.22. The source says the opposite: awkward positions arise \"only when an exercise ... fails to take into consideration the appropriate criteria\" (PDF 256 / p.245).\n3. **Accentuated joint angle entry**: it quotes the \"incongruous and artificial\" positions but drops that same \"However, this occurs only when...\" sentence. It needs adding back.\n4. **Skater case study**: in Table 4.2, Class 1 factor IV is 2.7, which is smaller than factor V (8.9) and breaks the factor order. It may be a misprint for 12.7. The entry should mark 2.7 as unclear and stop quoting the \"2.7 to 36.5\" jump.\n5. **High jumper case study**: \"less to plantarflexor power\" must be labelled \"Inference:\". The book reports a smaller factor share, not a cut in training.\n6. **Parachute tradeoffs**: \"heavy athletes, athletes returning from lower-limb injury\" must be labelled \"Inference:\". The book names no population.\n7. **Boxer vs shot putter**: \"full recovery\" is not in the source. Label it or drop it.\n8. **Parachute sizing**: \"standard fluid mechanics\" is the writer's uncited claim. Use the author's own \"(actually the square of the velocity)\" plus a labelled inference.\n9. **`_book.md`**: the Chapter 4 parent row still says \"in progress | 6\", while the batch note says Chapter 4 is complete.\n\n**Known source oddities:**\n- Fig 4.21, the \"6% ... only 7%\" sentence, the 4.3.3 effort rule and the aerobic/anaerobic antagonism are all handled honestly.\n- The Equation 4.1 and impulse wording quirks are recorded correctly, but the power entry has the separate physics error in fix 1.\n- I confirmed the Pattengale & Holloszy 1967 citation myself (PubMed 6036801, a treadmill-running study), so the entry's `contested` rating stands.\n- The writer's Table 4.1 and 4.2 column sums are correct: about 79/81% and 88/89%.\n\n**Other checks:**\n- I opened every figure, table and equation page as an image.\n- Every \"Eric's baseline:\" quote matches `method-baseline.md` at its cited line.\n- All wikilinks resolve, and every file has the six section headers with no other em dash.\n- There are no duplicates in the vault. The only possible missing idea is OBLA as the practical endurance target (PDF 260 / p.249), which is optional.\n\nAs the coordinator asked, page renders went to `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/_renders/` (gitignored) instead of the scratchpad."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":344,"cache_read_input_tokens":196152,"output_tokens":1180,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":344},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1180,"cache_read_input_tokens":196152,"cache_creation_input_tokens":344,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":344,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type